<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy approves Akros Attimo as new bank.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy approves Akros Attimo as new bank.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy has given a banking licence to Akros Attimo Sim SpA, and the new bank is set to start operations in January 1997.</p>
<p>An Akros statement said that its request has been approved by the central bank after a close evaluation of the project put forward by the company run by chairman Giovanni Pavese and managing director Marco Turrina.</p>
<p>The bank owns 100 percent of broker Akros Sim and is totally controlled by Akros Finanziaria SpA.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
